{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1453884-winter-ball-traditions","id":1453884,"title":"Winter Ball Traditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-30T19:30:21-07:00","id":1453884,"title":"Winter Ball Traditions","content":"So I'm looking to run a session set in a winter ball led by the Winter King and I'm wondering what sort of traditions would be fun for it, both with and without a mechanical benefit. Little superstitions and little ceremonies that can make it feel more magical and important and really emphasise what winter is about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T04:46:00-07:00","id":1453917,"title":"","content":"Well, everyone should wear masks of course. Maybe illusions hide their features. I think it'd help if you set out a basic premise first, as one winter court is not the same as another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T15:26:40-07:00","id":1453983,"title":"","content":"Lords of Summer from First Edition had a number of Court rituals. Two of the examples from Winter were a market where transactions were secret and anonymous (except to the Winter overseers) and a bonfire wherein members of the freehold were invited to burn symbols representing their secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}